 "title": "The Wall",
 "country": "UK",
 "notes": "Gatefold sleeve with plastic 'sticker' that adheres to the sleeve, but is not permanently stuck on. \nBand members are listed inside the sleeve, below the songwriting credits. \nInner sleeves also feature the \"Wall\" design with lyrics (graphics by Gerald Scarfe). \nThe track order on the inners is not the same as featured on the album. \n \nRecorded at \nSuperbear Miravel, France \nProducers Workshop Los Angeles \nC.B.S. New York \nbetween April and November 1979. \n \nThree different catalog numbers, one for the album and one for each disc: \nSHDW 411 = album \nOC-158 63410 SHSP 4111 = disc 1 \nOC-158 63411 SHSP 4112 = disc 2 \n\nAccordingly the system of matrix numbering this repress was pressed in 1980-1982.\n\nYou can view the UK first edition here: [r27371856]\n\nAll  runouts data is stamped",
